  "reviewNotes": "PDF page4 and front/rear/native-top source views. Native datum17mm; maximum46.4216mm. Five measured cap components at44mm provide independent loaf centres/radii and brown crust tones. Open cloth locations[11,1.5] and[15,12] have heights41.895699/41.680256mm; the crust starts42.1mm above that fabric. Scored cuts remain native geometry and baked normal/AO. Sage cloth includes the upper surface and drooping end panels, while two distinct counter tiers retain oriented timber. Left stand point measures[-10,0,25.785656]mm; right half is blocked. Compare the upper cloth/loaf boundary and each scored silhouette in both tiers. First top-view revealed crust on a raised cloth fold. Final crust domains follow the covariance-measured rotated cap footprints of all five loaves, expanded by only.35mm; individual elliptical masks keep the raised cloth green. Reverse review exposed a green patch on the widest lower flank of the front oval loaf; its full footprint clearance is.7mm beyond the44mm cap instead of.35mm. Other loaf masks remain unchanged.",
